    "field": "Emergent constraints on cloud feedbacks",
    "problem": "Predictions of future climate, particularly climate sensitivity, diverge significantly across models due to uncertainties in representing cloud feedbacks, and existing methods are insufficient to narrow the range of outcomes and assess model credibility.",
    "method": "This paper reviews the use of emergent constraints\u2014physically explainable empirical relationships between current climate observables and future climate predictions across model ensembles\u2014to reduce uncertainty in long-term predictions of cloud feedbacks and climate sensitivity.",
    "task": "The task is to review and assess proposed emergent constraints for cloud feedbacks, discussing criteria for their credibility and their potential to reduce uncertainty in long-term climate predictions from climate models.",
